																		Jam post
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/fieldstone" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1436137); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1436137&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608196064" alt="fieldstone" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1436137)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/fieldstone" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1436137); return false;" >fieldstone</a></span> <span class="odate time_1518900151 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">17 Feb 2018 20:42</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3713474">
									

<p>Go big or go home, right?</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">on&nbsp;the&nbsp;use&nbsp;of&nbsp;these&nbsp;characters</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>These are the same characters, and a very similar overall plotline, to the compliance team orientation I was going on and on about for months and never got past the first draft with. I feel like this is legitimately a new article, as everything here was new-written in a deadline-induced frenzy after the theme was announced (the plot is similar because these people bust into offices and interrogate chumps all the time). If the similarity to a previously drafted article disqualifies this from the contest, I understand - this was still the most fun I've ever had writing for the site.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>For context, these people are in a 1950s-ish time period where they don't have computers yet. Doctor Blank is the same character from <a href="/parts">this story</a>, with a new name and new lease on life. Hope you have as much fun with this as I did.</p>
<p>Edit - whoops, changed a character's name from Tran to Cooper at some point but missed it a few times in proofreading. That's just part of jam life I guess.</p>

							</div>

								
